//  PETPORTS -- ATTACH THE COVERAGE OVERLAY TO THE PLAYER
//
//  arch.port.coverage: the overlay runs on the PLAYER because every useful
//  question about coverage is a question about neighbours, and an object can
//  only ever draw its own box.
//
//  deploymentConfig/scripts AND NOT genericScriptContexts, for now.
//
//  genericScriptContexts is the cleaner 1.4+ hook -- a named context of our
//  own, no chaining, and no clobbering of other mods' player scripts. It is
//  probably where this ends up. It is not where it starts, because the only
//  player-script `localAnimator` use anyone can point at in the wild runs in
//  the shared deployment context, and this hook is now MEASURED to work
//  (2026-09-04, fact.port.drawablespace). Moving it is a separate change with
//  its own test, not a tidy-up to fold into a working build.
//
//  APPENDED WITH `/-`, so we load last and the init/update/uninit chain in the
//  script always has an original to call.

[
	{
		"op" : "add",
		"path" : "/deploymentConfig/scripts/-",
		"value" : "/scripts/lofty_petports/petports_coverageoverlay.lua"
	}
]
